Cardinal guessed keys for 2 tables that keep 4 models from being checked, and 1 reference. It uses none of them until dbt confirms them on your data.

  app.customers  one row per customer_id
                 why: customer_id is named like the table's id, and orders_with_customer joins on it
                 lets Cardinal check 2 models that depend on it

  app.events     one row per event_id
                 why: event_id is named like the table's id
                 lets Cardinal check 2 models that depend on it

  app.orders     every customer_id is in app.customers.customer_id
                 why: orders_with_customer joins app.orders to app.customers on it, and drops the rows that have no match
                 lets Cardinal prove orders_with_customer keeps every row of app.orders

Wrote 3 tests to tests/cardinal/.
Next: dbt test --select tag:cardinal
Then run cardinal check. Each guess dbt passes counts as a known key or reference,
labeled as a guess; each one dbt fails is dropped and never guessed again.
